      "typical_award_size": "The 2008 Density Bonus Ordinance was replaced by Chapter C.12 (Density Bonus for Affordable Housing Developments) of the new Zoning Ordinance, Title XIII, adopted September 2, 2025 and effective October 2, 2025. It grants density bonuses, incentives, waivers and parking ratios per state law, and allowed incentives include waived, reduced or deferred City fees (plan check, permit and development impact fees), direct financial aid by loan or grant, and density beyond state law, with additional incentives decided case by case; eligibility requires full on-site compliance with the 15 percent Affordable Housing Ordinance. The Housing Element also states the City provides fee deferrals for projects with on-site affordable units and commits to explore fee deferrals, reductions or waivers for 100 percent affordable projects in the Metro and Gateway-Main Street specific plan areas (Program 20). No standalone fee waiver schedule or dollar amount is published.",
